;; The classes of bin/java-check's non-passing tests (doc/classes/JAVA-CONFORMANCE-SURVEY.md, §6.1,
;; "As built: JC1"): every test of test/java/check-LEVEL.edn that does not pass falls into the first
;; class whose :level is its level (or that has none) and one of whose :match regexps finds its
;; "RESULT REASON" (as bin/java-check writes them in .tmp/java-check/results.tsv); a test no class
;; takes fails the check (java.check/report). :kind says whose the work is: :world (a JDK class or
;; member jrt lacks, deferred, JCS9 (b): JC6 ranks them), :design (out of the Go build for good,
;; J2G-SPEC §12), :interp (the interpreter's bugs and limits: JC4), :analysis (the Java forms'
;; analysis refusing forms javac accepted: JC5, JCS11 (c)), :repl (the REPL's model: JC4, JCS8),
;; :repr-java (the converter: JCS12), :j2g (j2g's translation: the compiled level, JC2), :javac (javac
;; on Arbace's own Java, overlay/jdk/javac: its command line and file manager; the diagnostics level,
;; JC3), :speed, :harness (the check's runner, not Arbace), :other. A class nobody decided yet has
;; :decided :pending and names its :proposal.
;; Read with the Clojure reader.
[
 {:id :speed
  :title "speed: beyond the check's limit (20 s an action, the definition included)"
  :kind :speed
  :why "the interpreter is 5-200 times slower than HotSpot (CLASSFORMS-REPL §6); HotSpot's JIT tests loop 10^5-10^6 times to warm the JIT"
  :decided "survey §6.1, JCS10 (a)"
  :match [#"^timeout "]}
 {:id :read-failed
  :title "not interpreted or compiled: the read level failed (the test's class at that level)"
  :kind :harness
  :why "no forms to interpret or translate; the read level's result says why"
  :decided "As built: JC1"
  :match [#"^unread "]}
 ;; the tests whose result depends on timing or chance, by name (JCS71 (a)): bin/java-check runs a
 ;; would-be regression again once, and a test whose second run passes is reported flaky; it is no
 ;; regression when a class here names it, and in no class (the check failing) until one does. A
 ;; class of the level: a test flaky at one level is not at another (Test8267042's interp output
 ;; differs every run, LockStep's interp level fails to load ObjectInputStream every run)
 {:id :flaky
  :title "flaky: the result depends on the threads' timing or a Random's draw; passed when run again (JCS71 (a)), or fails by chance"
  :kind :harness
  :level :compiled
  :why "jdk/java/lang/ref/EnqueuePollRace counts the references the collector has enqueued (99 of 100 once, on the loaded host; JC6); compiler/c1/Test8267042 prints as two threads interleave (174 bytes against the JDK's 137 on the loaded host); jdk/java/util/List/LockStep serializes a list when its Random says so (maybe(4)), reaching ObjectOutputStream, cut (D6), by chance: both passed in JC2's compiled run and not in JC2b's"
  :decided "JCS71 (a) (doc/classes/JAVA-CONFORMANCE-SURVEY.md, \"Decided (2026-10-25): JCS70-JCS79\", \"As built: harness follow-ups\")"
  :tests ["t03289" "t04819" "t05565"]}
 ;; the print level (REAP5, doc/FULL-SUPPORT-SURVEY.md, "As built: REAP5"; RPS9 (a)): a test's first
 ;; step not passing, of print, javac, forms, text, classes (java.print, test/java/print.ae); here,
 ;; before the classes of no level, whose regexps would take the printed Java's messages
 {:id :print-release
  :title "print: javac on Arbace refuses --release N (no ct.sym in its platform), as for the original (the classes level)"
  :kind :world
  :level :print
  :why "the test's @compile options hold --release 8 or 17; javac on Arbace attributes against the JDK build tree's exploded modules, which hold no ct.sym (JAVA-CONFORMANCE-SURVEY §5.5): the printed Java is refused as the original is"
  :decided "JCS50 (a), as :read-platform and :diag-release (doc/classes/JAVA-CONFORMANCE-SURVEY.md, \"Decided (2026-10-25): JCS50-JCS55\")"
  :match [#"release version \d+ not supported"]}
 {:id :print-type-arguments
  :title "print: javac rejects the printed Java for want of Java's type arguments in code (inference, captured and type-variable types, generic conversions)"
  :kind :repr-java
  :level :print
  :why "Java's type arguments in code are not in the forms (SPEC §1, principle 4), and where the original's typing needed them (a generic method's inference from wildcard-typed arguments, a captured type's cast, an explicit type argument, a lambda's parameter types through generic calls, a raw array of a generic type; RemoveMicroBenchmark's Stream.<Collection<Integer>>of(...), whose lambdas' parameters javac then types Object: cannot find symbol, REAP5b) the printer's casts do not recover them: the conformance corpus's kin of the 39 jdk files of bin/repr-java roundtrip (PRINTER-NOTES.md, \"javac rejects the printed Java\")"
  :decided "RPS9 (a): deferred until JFS75 (b)'s model carries type arguments (doc/FULL-SUPPORT-SURVEY.md, \"Decided (2026-10-24): RPS1-RPS17\")"
  :tests ["t05474"]
  :match [#"^fail javac rejects the printed Java: .*(inference variable|cannot infer type|cannot be applied to given types|no suitable (method|constructor)|CAP#|incomparable types|is ambiguous|bad return type in|is not a functional interface|incompatible types: invalid method reference|cannot be converted to [\w.$]+<|incompatible types: Object cannot be converted to|incompatible types: [A-Z]\d* cannot be converted|cannot be converted to [A-Z]\d*(\s|$))"]}
 {:id :print-forms
  :title "print: the printed Java read again gives other forms (a literal's sign, width or rounding; a cast or a local's tag; a restructured if, loop, label, try or temporary)"
  :kind :repr-java
  :level :print
  :why "the converter does not read the printer's Java to the forms it printed from: a negative literal (-1.0f reads as (float (unchecked-negate-float ...))), an int widened to float (16777217 as 1.6777217E7), a literal's overload ((long 1)), a cast the converter adds or drops (.next of a raw Iterator, an Integer's .intValue), a local's :mutable tag, when against if, a loop's or label's name, a pattern's temporary; since REAP5b also the tests whose printed Java javac refused before (RPS60-RPS62, 21): the casts an assignment context needs where the converter's forms type a box otherwise than its declaration ((int) x.byteValue() into a Byte read as an Integer, RPS85), a pattern binding renamed where the converter's nesting of a && chain rebinds it (i_1, RPS86), a long literal's negation, a float constant's digits, an unexpanded temporary (o_3): bin/repr-java roundtrip's forms level, whose known differences are the same kinds (PRINTER-NOTES.md, \"The round trip\")"
  :decided "RPS64 (a): deferred, decided per kind (literals and casts with JC5's converter and the printer, restructurings by design) (doc/FULL-SUPPORT-SURVEY.md, \"Decided (2026-10-25): RPS60-RPS78\")"
  :proposal "RPS64"
  :match [#"^differ forms: "]}
 {:id :print-overload-cast
  :title "print: the forms lose a cast that chooses an overload (v((Object) \"s\") read as v(\"s\")): the printed Java calls another method"
  :kind :repr-java
  :level :print
  :why "the JLS corpus's Overloads: the converter drops the cast to Object of a String argument (it is a widening, javac's attribution keeps it only to choose v(Object)), so the forms, the printed Java and the interpreter (:interp-jls) call v(String); found by the print level's class files (invokestatic v:(Ljava/lang/Object;) against v:(Ljava/lang/String;)), the forms equal F1 (they lost it at the read)"
  :decided "RPS65 (a): deferred to JC5, the converter keeping a cast that changes javac's overload choice (doc/FULL-SUPPORT-SURVEY.md, \"Decided (2026-10-25): RPS60-RPS78\")"
  :proposal "RPS65"
  :tests ["t03216"]}
 {:id :print-classes
  :title "print: the printed Java's class files differ from the original's by what the forms do not record (a value's control flow, a local's initializer, fall-through, an increment's place, the loops' restructuring, the order of code or of the constant pool)"
  :kind :design
  :level :print
  :why "the forms record no source's choice of ?: against if or of a switch expression against a statement, Java's default value of a local written or not, a switch's fall-through (the following arms' code repeated), i++'s place, a loop's continue against the if's other arm: javac compiles the printed Java to other code of the same meaning, as for bin/repr-java roundtrip's classes level (PRINTER-NOTES.md, \"The class files\"; the forms level of this test passes: the printed Java holds the forms)"
  :decided "RPS9 (a): print's class files against the original's under bin/repr-java roundtrip's classes (doc/FULL-SUPPORT-SURVEY.md, \"Decided (2026-10-24): RPS1-RPS17\"); PRINTER-NOTES.md, \"The class files\" (the rest by design)"
  :match [#"^differ classes: "]}
 {:id :diag-release
  :title "javac on Arbace: --release N, any N (no ct.sym in its platform)"
  :kind :world
  :level :diagnostics
  :why "javac on Arbace attributes against the JDK build tree's exploded modules (jdk/javac/platform.sha256), which hold no ct.sym, the releases' signatures --release reads (survey §5.5): \"release version N not supported\", status 2, for 8-26"
  :decided "JCS50 (a), with (b) first: deferred, --release 26 as -source/-target 26, then the pinned ct.sym served as JDKPlatformProvider does (doc/classes/JAVA-CONFORMANCE-SURVEY.md, \"Decided (2026-10-25): JCS50-JCS55\")"
  :proposal "JCS50"
  :match [#"release version \d+ not supported"]}
 {:id :diag-processors
  :title "javac on Arbace: annotation processors from class files (\"Could not instantiate an instance of processor\", proc.processor.cant.instantiate)"
  :kind :world
  :level :diagnostics
  :why "a processor built by @build is a class file on the class path; javac on Arbace has no class loader to define it (J2G-SPEC §12: class loading out of the Go build), so the processing tests stop at the processor's instantiation"
  :decided "JCS51 (a): deferred, processors given as sources defined by the interpreter and handed to javac as instances (doc/classes/JAVA-CONFORMANCE-SURVEY.md, \"Decided (2026-10-25): JCS50-JCS55\")"
  :proposal "JCS51"
  :match [#"cant\.instantiate" #"Could not instantiate an instance of processor"]}
 {:id :diag-doclint
  :title "javac on Arbace: -Xdoclint (compiler.warn.doclint.not.available)"
  :kind :world
  :level :diagnostics
  :why "doclint is jdk.javadoc's (jdk.javadoc.internal.doclint), not in javac's world (jdk/javac: jdk.compiler, java.compiler); javac then warns and checks no comments (survey §5.5)"
  :decided "JCS52 (a): deferred, jdk.javadoc's doclint added to javac's world (doc/classes/JAVA-CONFORMANCE-SURVEY.md, \"Decided (2026-10-25): JCS50-JCS55\")"
  :proposal "JCS52"
  :match [#"doclint\.not\.available"]}
 {:id :diag-closed-world
  :title "javac on Arbace: a JDK class outside javac's closed world reached (java.lang.annotation.Annotation, java.lang.Module): the compiler's crash"
  :kind :world
  :level :diagnostics
  :why "javac's world is closed (j2g, J2G-SPEC §4.1); Check's leak check of a --patch-module java.base and the processing environment's processor loader (JavacProcessingEnvironment.initProcessorLoader) reach classes j2g left out"
  :decided "As built: JC3 (deferred, JCS9 (b): JC6 ranks the world's classes)"
  :match [#"is not in the closed world"]}
 {:id :diag-file-manager
  :title "javac on Arbace's file manager (jdk.internal.jrt.javac.FileManager, not javac's BaseFileManager): file names in full in raw diagnostics, no source.no.system.modules.path warning for -source N, -source 8's platform classes, a module-info's error twice"
  :kind :javac
  :level :diagnostics
  :why "javac's raw diagnostics print a PathFileObject's short name and other file objects' getName (Bar.class against .../classes/Bar.class); Arguments warns source.no.system.modules.path only for a BaseFileManager's default system modules; -source 8 looks java.lang up on the boot class path, which the platform's file manager does not serve; Log's de-duplication keys on the file object, two of which name one module-info.java"
  :decided "JCS53 (a): deferred, Arbace's Main calling javac's Main.compile with Arbace's file manager, file objects as PathFileObject (doc/classes/JAVA-CONFORMANCE-SURVEY.md, \"Decided (2026-10-25): JCS50-JCS55\")"
  :proposal "JCS53"
  :tests ["t07442" "t07462"]
  :match [#"misc\.bad\.source\.file\.header: langtools/" #"classfile: RUN/" #"source\.no\.system\.modules\.path" #"Unable to find package java\.lang in platform classes" #"source value 8 is obsolete"]}
 {:id :diag-command-line
  :title "javac on Arbace's command line (jdk.internal.jrt.javac.Main, javac's API underneath, not javac's Main): -XDexpectKeys, the error count after a plug-in error, -encoding ascii, --module-path a jar"
  :kind :javac
  :level :diagnostics
  :why "javac on Arbace's Main parses the file manager's options itself and calls JavacTool.getTask (As built: JN3): what com.sun.tools.javac.main.Main.compile does beyond the task (the expected keys' report, the count when the task stops early) is missing, and the file manager refuses the encodings and module paths it does not serve"
  :decided "JCS53 (a): deferred, as :diag-file-manager; non-UTF-8 -encoding and a jar on --module-path stay refused (doc/classes/JAVA-CONFORMANCE-SURVEY.md, \"Decided (2026-10-25): JCS50-JCS55\")"
  :proposal "JCS53"
  :tests ["t06660" "t07527"]
  :match [#"unsupported on Arbace: "]}
 {:id :read-platform
  :title "javac on Arbace: options its platform lacks (--release N without ct.sym, the charset alias utf8)"
  :kind :world
  :why "javac on Arbace attributes against the JDK build tree's modules, no ct.sym (JAVA-CONFORMANCE-SURVEY §5.5); jrt's charsets know UTF-8, not every alias"
